stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR

  state "Task: completed" as task_completed
  state "Task: running (original owner)" as task_running
  state "Task: blocked (original owner)" as task_blocked

  [*] --> requested
  requested --> validating_inputs: reserve budget + resolve sealed inputs
  requested --> cancelled: policy or owner cancels
  validating_inputs --> rejected: invalid hash, rubric, or capability
  validating_inputs --> expired: capability or request expires
  validating_inputs --> running: create non-owning reviewer Run
  running --> submitted: Review record emitted
  running --> cancelled: authorized cancellation
  running --> expired: review deadline
  submitted --> rejected: provenance or read-only validation fails
  submitted --> accepted: Review record structurally valid

  state accepted {
    [*] --> verdict
    state verdict <<choice>>
    verdict --> pass
    verdict --> fail
    verdict --> abstain
  }

  pass --> task_completed: all completion gates satisfied
  fail --> task_running: correctable finding
  fail --> task_blocked: policy, permission, or safety finding
  abstain --> task_blocked: replacement reviewer or human needed

  task_completed --> [*]
  task_running --> [*]
  task_blocked --> [*]
  rejected --> [*]
  expired --> [*]
  cancelled --> [*]

  note right of running
    The reviewer does not acquire
    the Task ownership lease.
    Inputs are sealed and read-only.
  end note

  note right of accepted
    accepted validates the Review record.
    pass or fail is the artifact verdict.
  end note
